{{also|Proletariat|prolétariat|proletariát}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|proletariate}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|prolétariat|}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|proletarius||a man whose only wealth is his offspring, or whose sole service to the state is as father}}, from {{m|la|proles||offspring, posterity}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|'prōlĭʹtârēət}}, {{IPA|/ˌpɹoʊlɪˈtɛəɹi.ət/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-ca-proletariat.oga|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[working class]] or lower [[class]].
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|page=173
|year=1906
|author=Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels
|title=Manifesto of the Communist Party
|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=s2iEeCJAlusC
|passage="Of all the classes that stand face to face with the bourgeoisie to day the '''proletariat''' alone is a really revolutionary class."}}
# The [[wage earner]]s collectively, excluding [[salaried]] workers.
# {{lb|en|history}} In ancient Rome, the lowest [[class]] of [[citizen]]s, who had no [[property]]; "regarded as contributing nothing to the state but offspring" (OED, 1992).

